# Keep source files byte-identical across Windows, Linux, and macOS runners.
# In particular, gofmt treats CRLF checkouts as different from canonical Go
# formatting, so Go sources must always be checked out with LF endings.
*.go text eol=lf
*.mod text eol=lf
*.sum text eol=lf
*.m text eol=lf
*.h text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
